{
 "_comment": [
  "tests/i18n/dump.html opens every surface below (GE0a, notes/claude/round0/ge0a.md; H: notes/english-option-design.md §3.3).",
  "q: the query after /ui/index.html? (dump.html adds mock=1 mockreset=1 mockStatic=1 theme=light lang= i18ncheck=1 i18nstop=).",
  "wait: logical ms the page runs (its stop time; default below). seed: mock settings put in localStorage first (no mockreset).",
  "do: harness actions after the stop time, for G surfaces without an ?open= hook: [{click|contextmenu: CSS selector, nth?: 0 first, -1 last, wait?: logical ms more (default 1500)}].",
  "Hooks: ?open= (Alles; GE1a/H's E1: Verkenner, Taakbeheer and Schijven menus and dialogs), ?page=, ?place=, ?path=, ?select=, ?properties=, ?volume=, ?disk=, ?picker=, ?tabs=, ?path=/?uninstall= (installer), ?query= (Standaard-apps). GE1a added H's 17 E1 surfaces (H's ids) and three GNOME states of the mocks (settings-gnome.display, settings-gnome.clipboard and the removed shell.clipboard.unsupported: what the Rust host reports under GNOME). D-G70 removed the HTML shell and desktop surfaces (shell, shell.*, desktop, desktop.*; the native GTK 4 shell native/shell replaced them), so every surface is surface=app.",
  "The settings.* ids (but settings.search and the settings.installed.* actions) must be exactly the pages of vendor/ui/js/apps/settings/registry.js, the taskmgr.* ids the tabs of taskmgr/main.js PAGE_IDS (tests/i18n/test_ge0a.py).",
  "Variants of a page that are not a registry page use another prefix (settings-gnome.*, taskmgr-dialog.*), so the settings.*/taskmgr.* rule above holds.",
  "settings-update.<id>: the Windows Update page in every mock state of mock/update.js (?updateScenario=, the ids of notes/claude/windows-update-gnome.md §9.3 plus H27/H28, and text variants with a letter, e.g. H05b, plus R06; GW3). Later steps add theirs through notes/claude/surfaces-additions-<step>.json.",
  "settings-update-history.<id> / settings-update-advanced.<id>: the two Windows Update subpages in every mock state of mock/update.js (?updateScenario=S…, GW4: S01-S02b history, S03-S03i advanced options; R3-UI: S03j/S03k refreshes held by snapd); the registry pages settings.update-history / settings.update-advanced show the defaults (S01, S03).",
  "settings-check.<name> (R3-UI fix round): behaviour a text dump does not show. probe: checks after the actions, [{disabled|inview: CSS selector, nth?}], each one line '# probe <check> <selector>: true|false|none' (dump.html). language-EN: a hand-edited language the dropdown resolves as C1 does (Nederlands); restartall-dry / -sent: the update page's Win11 Shell restart button after a dry-run answer (usable) and after a real one (?mockRestartAll=live: disabled until the page is built again, gx1.md §7 decision 1); recovery-link / -none: Updategeschiedenis' Herstel row scrolls Update en herstel to its backup and reset group (the control without the link: not in view).",
  "settings-update-prompt.<id>: the \"Nieuwe Ubuntu-versies\" row of the Update page in the mock states M01-M04 of mock/update.js (?updateScenario=M…, GW5: M01 normal with the /bin/sh InfoBar of a PC without the root helper (today), M01b never, M02 lts on an interim release, M03 overridden by a release-upgrades.d file, M04 a change waiting for Ubuntu's password dialog without the root helper (the ComboBox disabled, the InfoBar stays), M04b a change with the root helper and a dismissed password dialog); the page itself is idle (H01). Not under settings-update.: test_update_mock_rows.py pairs that prefix with the [HR] scenario ids.",
  "settings-update-card.<id>: the feature-update card \"Ubuntu 26.10 is beschikbaar\" of the Update page in the mock states C01-C16 of mock/update.js (?updateScenario=C…, GW6, design §3.5 and §9.3 plus letters: C01 not offered (no card), C02 checking, C03 ok, C03b an LTS offer, C04 warn with \"Let op voordat je upgradet\" opened, C05 hold (GNOME 51 named), C05b hold by releases.json alone, C05c hold with \"Toch upgraden…\", C05d its warning start dialog, C06 blocked, C07/C07b updatesFirst, C08 rebootFirst, C09 the start dialog on battery and metered with the English-first line, C10 running next to our own job, C11 waiting, C12 ubuntuHold, C13/C13b/C13c unknown (apt, offline, metered), C14 startFailed, C14b after Retry, C15 ended, C16 hold after the postponement, C16b its live click). Not under settings-update.: test_update_mock_rows.py pairs that prefix with the [HR] scenario ids."
 ],
